    <!-- Q&A Page -->
    <string name="qa_title">Q&amp;A</string>
    <string name="qa_network_permission_title">Does PocketVault access the Internet?</string>
    <string name="qa_network_permission_content">No. PocketVault does not request Android Internet permission and includes no analytics, advertising, telemetry, or crash-reporting SDK. Vault data is processed locally. Data leaves the app only when you explicitly export or share a backup.</string>
    <string name="qa_data_security_title">I forgot my Master Password. Can you reset it for me?</string>
    <string name="qa_data_security_content">No. PocketVault has no account, server, recovery key, or password-reset backdoor. A key derived from your master password locally unwraps the random key that encrypts the vault. If you lose the master password and biometric convenience unlock is unavailable, the vault cannot be recovered. Keep the password safe. Older backups require the password that protected them when they were created.</string>
    <string name="qa_offline_usage_title">Where is my data stored?</string>
    <string name="qa_offline_usage_content" formatted="false">The current vault and automatic backup history are stored in PocketVault\'s private application storage. Clearing app data or uninstalling removes those local files. Backups you exported or shared are outside the app and must be deleted separately from every destination.</string>
    <string name="how_is_my_data_protected_title">How is my data protected?</string>
    <string name="how_is_my_data_protected_content">We use the Google Tink cryptographic library.\n • Encryption: AES-256-GCM-HKDF (Streaming AEAD).\n • Derivation: New and re-keyed vaults use PBKDF2-SHA256 with 600,000 iterations.\nA strong master password makes offline attempts substantially more expensive, but no software or password can guarantee absolute security.</string>

